# M6: Benchmarks

<!-- Generated from m6.md.in by `make bench-docs`: every number comes from
bench/results/*.json. Edit the template, not m6.md. -->

## What was built

A benchmark harness in `bench/` and a measured optimization pass over the engine.

- **Workloads.** A seeded generator (`bench/lib/workload.cpp`) produces two order flows
  with every risk limit set: *narrow* (fixed mid, prices within a few ticks: few, deep
  levels) and *wide* (drifting mid, prices spread over thousands of ticks, a few far
  away: many shallow levels). It decides each command from a shadow `Engine`, so cancels
  and replaces target orders that are really resting.
- **End-to-end replay** (`mf-bench-replay`): millions of commands through a fresh `Engine`
  per repetition; throughput timed as one batch, latency timed per command into an
  HdrHistogram; warm-up excluded; heap allocations per command counted.
- **Microbenchmarks** (`mf-bench-micro`, Google Benchmark): add, cancel, replace, match
  at one level and across levels, the risk check, and an add through the whole engine.
- **Tooling**: `make bench` writes `bench/results/*.json` and renders the docs from them;
  `make bench-ab` compares two tagged builds in interleaved rounds; `make gate` runs every
  correctness check an optimization must pass; CI smoke-runs it all without judging speed.
- **Optimizations**, each one commit between two tags, measured before and after:
  see `bench/OPTIMIZATIONS.md`.

